const LB_FORMS={"lb-intake":{"name":"Lash & brow client intake","qs":[{"id":"lb-intake-1","label":"Full name","type":"Short text","required":true},{"id":"lb-intake-2","label":"Date of birth","type":"Date","required":false},{"id":"lb-intake-3","label":"Mobile phone","type":"Short text","required":false},{"id":"lb-intake-4","label":"Email","type":"Short text","required":false},{"id":"lb-intake-5","label":"Address","type":"Short text","required":false},{"id":"lb-intake-6","label":"Emergency contact & relationship","type":"Short text","required":false},{"id":"lb-intake-7","label":"Their phone","type":"Short text","required":false},{"id":"lb-intake-8","label":"How did you hear about us?","type":"Short text","required":false},{"id":"lb-intake-9","label":"Best way to reach you","type":"Single select","required":false,"options":["Text","Email","Call"]},{"id":"lb-intake-10","label":"OK to text you reminders?","type":"Yes / No","required":false},{"id":"lb-intake-11","label":"Which service are you booking? Check all that apply","type":"Multiple choice","required":true,"options":["Classic lash extensions","Hybrid / volume lashes","Lash fill","Lash extension removal","Lash lift & tint","Brow lamination","Brow tint or henna","Brow wax / shaping"]},{"id":"lb-intake-12","label":"Had lashes, a lift or tint before? If yes, what and when","type":"Short text","required":false},{"id":"lb-intake-13","label":"Any reaction before (itching, swelling, lash loss)? If yes, describe","type":"Short text","required":false},{"id":"lb-intake-14","label":"Wearing extensions now?","type":"Single select","required":false,"options":["No","Mine","Another artist's"]},{"id":"lb-intake-15","label":"Lash lift or brow lamination in the past 8 weeks?","type":"Yes / No","required":false},{"id":"lb-intake-16","label":"What look would you love? Anything you want to avoid?","type":"Long text","required":false},{"id":"lb-intake-17","label":"Eyes & health: Some answers mean a waiting period or your doctor's OK first. Your answers stay confidential. Check anything that applies to you.","type":"Contraindications","required":false,"items":["I wear contact lenses","Eye infection, stye, pink eye or blepharitis now","Dry, watery or very sensitive eyes","Eye surgery (LASIK, cataract) in the past 3 months","Glaucoma, or I use glaucoma eye drops","Lash serum (e.g. bimatoprost) in the past 3 months","Lash or brow hair loss (alopecia, trichotillomania)","Thyroid condition or big hormone changes","Chemotherapy now or in the past year","Pregnant or breastfeeding","Eczema or psoriasis near eyes or brows","Sunburn, rash, cut or broken skin in the area","Botox near brows or eyes in the past 2 weeks","Peel, laser or microneedling in the past 2 weeks","Semi-permanent brows or liner in the past 6 weeks","Epilepsy or seizures","Trouble lying still with eyes closed for 2 hours","Diabetes or an autoimmune condition","Recent surgery or a hospital stay","Any other medical condition"]},{"id":"lb-intake-18","label":"If you checked anything, please explain (dates, medication, doctor)","type":"Long text","required":false},{"id":"lb-intake-19","label":"Are you allergic or sensitive to any of these? Check all that apply","type":"Multiple choice","required":false,"options":["Lash glue (cyanoacrylate)","Superglue or nail glue","Hair dye (PPD)","Henna or brow tint","Perm or lift solution","Latex","Medical or surgical tape","Fragrance","None that I know of"]},{"id":"lb-intake-20","label":"Reaction you had, and to what","type":"Short text","required":false},{"id":"lb-intake-21","label":"All medications you take, including prescriptions, eye drops and supplements","type":"Long text","required":false},{"id":"lb-intake-22","label":"Are you using, or have you recently used, any of these? They can affect waxing, lifts and retention. Never stop a prescribed medication without your doctor's OK.","type":"Contraindications","required":false,"items":["Isotretinoin (Accutane) in the past 6 months","Retinoid cream (tretinoin, adapalene)","Retinol, AHA or BHA near brows","Blood thinners or daily aspirin","Lash serum with bimatoprost","Glaucoma eye drops"]},{"id":"lb-intake-23","label":"Sleep position","type":"Single select","required":false,"options":["Back","Side","Face-down"]},{"id":"lb-intake-24","label":"Skin type","type":"Single select","required":false,"options":["Dry","Normal","Oily"]},{"id":"lb-intake-25","label":"Workouts / sauna","type":"Single select","required":false,"options":["Rarely","Weekly","Daily"]},{"id":"lb-intake-26","label":"Eye makeup","type":"Single select","required":false,"options":["Daily","Sometimes","Never"]},{"id":"lb-intake-27","label":"Oil cleanser","type":"Single select","required":false,"options":["Yes","No near eyes"]},{"id":"lb-intake-28","label":"Rub your eyes","type":"Single select","required":false,"options":["Often","Rarely"]},{"id":"lb-intake-29","label":"Swim or hot tub?","type":"Yes / No","required":false},{"id":"lb-intake-30","label":"Events coming in the next 4 weeks","type":"Short text","required":false},{"id":"lb-intake-31","label":"My answers are true and complete. I'll update you if my health or medications change.","type":"Yes / No","required":true},{"id":"lb-intake-32","label":"Results vary with my natural hair, skin, hormones and aftercare. No exact result is promised.","type":"Yes / No","required":true},{"id":"lb-intake-33","label":"Reactions to lash glue, tint or solutions can happen, even after many problem-free visits.","type":"Yes / No","required":true},{"id":"lb-intake-34","label":"I'll follow my aftercare. Skipping it can shorten results or cause irritation or lash damage.","type":"Yes / No","required":true},{"id":"lb-intake-35","label":"I'll keep any waiting periods that apply to me and get my doctor's clearance if asked.","type":"Yes / No","required":true},{"id":"lb-intake-36","label":"I am 18 or older and will show a valid photo ID (or a parent or guardian signs per our policy).","type":"Yes / No","required":true},{"id":"lb-intake-37","label":"YOUR PRIVACY. Your information is kept confidential, stored securely and used only to provide your services. It is never shared without your written consent unless the law requires it. Records are kept 7 years. I have read this.","type":"Yes / No","required":true},{"id":"lb-intake-38","label":"I confirm the information above is accurate","type":"Signature","required":true}]},
"lb-lash-design":{"name":"Lash map & design approval","qs":[{"id":"lb-lash-design-1","label":"Client name","type":"Short text","required":true},{"id":"lb-lash-design-2","label":"Artist","type":"Short text","required":false},{"id":"lb-lash-design-3","label":"Client's right eye, lengths in mm (zone 5 outer to zone 1 inner)","type":"Short text","required":false},{"id":"lb-lash-design-4","label":"Client's left eye, lengths in mm (zone 1 inner to zone 5 outer)","type":"Short text","required":false},{"id":"lb-lash-design-5","label":"Style","type":"Single select","required":false,"options":["Natural","Open-eye","Cat eye","Doll","Squirrel"]},{"id":"lb-lash-design-6","label":"Type","type":"Single select","required":false,"options":["Classic","Hybrid","Volume"]},{"id":"lb-lash-design-7","label":"Curl","type":"Single select","required":false,"options":["J","B","C","CC","D","L/M"]},{"id":"lb-lash-design-8","label":"Diameter","type":"Single select","required":false,"options":["0.05","0.07","0.10","0.12","0.15","Other"]},{"id":"lb-lash-design-9","label":"Natural lashes","type":"Single select","required":false,"options":["Healthy","Fine or sparse","Short","Damaged"]},{"id":"lb-lash-design-10","label":"Eye shape","type":"Single select","required":false,"options":["Almond","Round","Hooded","Monolid","Downturned","Deep-set"]},{"id":"lb-lash-design-11","label":"Lash brand · type · adhesive · lot #","type":"Short text","required":false},{"id":"lb-lash-design-12","label":"Notes: inner corners, spikes, lower lashes, retention from last visit","type":"Long text","required":false},{"id":"lb-lash-design-13","label":"Before starting","type":"Multiple choice","required":false,"options":["Before photos taken","Contacts removed","Patch test done or waived"]},{"id":"lb-lash-design-14","label":"CLIENT APPROVAL. I've reviewed this lash map and chose my style, curl and lengths. I understand extensions must suit the strength of my natural lashes, so my artist may adjust length or thickness to protect them, and that my look can be refined at my next fill.","type":"Yes / No","required":true},{"id":"lb-lash-design-15","label":"Client signature","type":"Signature","required":true}]},
"lb-brow-design":{"name":"Brow shaping & design approval","qs":[{"id":"lb-brow-design-1","label":"Client name","type":"Short text","required":true},{"id":"lb-brow-design-2","label":"Artist","type":"Short text","required":false},{"id":"lb-brow-design-3","label":"Client's right brow (mm from center): start, arch, tail, arch height, start width, tail height","type":"Short text","required":false},{"id":"lb-brow-design-4","label":"Client's left brow (mm from center): start, arch, tail, arch height, start width, tail height","type":"Short text","required":false},{"id":"lb-brow-design-5","label":"Shape goal","type":"Single select","required":false,"options":["Natural","Soft arch","Straight","Lifted","Fluffy","Defined"]},{"id":"lb-brow-design-6","label":"Services","type":"Multiple choice","required":false,"options":["Lamination","Tint","Henna","Wax","Tweeze","Thread"]},{"id":"lb-brow-design-7","label":"Natural hair","type":"Single select","required":false,"options":["Blonde","Light brown","Dark brown","Black","Red","Gray"]},{"id":"lb-brow-design-8","label":"Undertone","type":"Single select","required":false,"options":["Cool","Neutral","Warm"]},{"id":"lb-brow-design-9","label":"Shade goal","type":"Short text","required":false},{"id":"lb-brow-design-10","label":"Product · shade and mix · lot # · processing time","type":"Short text","required":false},{"id":"lb-brow-design-11","label":"Before starting","type":"Multiple choice","required":false,"options":["Before photos taken","Shape mapped and approved","Patch test done or waived"]},{"id":"lb-brow-design-12","label":"CLIENT APPROVAL. I checked this mapped shape in the mirror and approve the shape, thickness and shade. Brows are sisters, not twins; tint and henna soften after day one, and removed hair takes weeks to regrow.","type":"Yes / No","required":true},{"id":"lb-brow-design-13","label":"Client signature","type":"Signature","required":true}]},
"lb-service-consent":{"name":"Lash & brow service consent","qs":[{"id":"lb-service-consent-1","label":"Client name","type":"Short text","required":true},{"id":"lb-service-consent-2","label":"Date of birth","type":"Date","required":false},{"id":"lb-service-consent-3","label":"Service(s) I'm consenting to","type":"Long text","required":true},{"id":"lb-service-consent-4","label":"ABOUT YOUR SERVICES. What these services are: Lash extensions, lifts, lamination, tinting and brow shaping are cosmetic. Results are temporary and need upkeep. During your visit: You lie still, eyes closed, for lash work. Opening them early can let fumes or solution in. Products used: Lash glue (cyanoacrylate), lift and lamination solutions, tints or henna, and wax. Each can cause a reaction. I have read this.","type":"Yes / No","required":true},{"id":"lb-service-consent-5","label":"POSSIBLE RISKS AND SIDE EFFECTS. Allergic reaction: puffy, itchy or red lids or skin from glue, tint or solution; it can start after many visits; Eye irritation: red, watery or stinging eyes from fumes or product, usually gone within a day; Infection: rare with clean tools and good aftercare; watch for discharge, swelling or pain; Natural lash or brow damage: from heavy extensions, over-processing, picking or pulling, or skipping fills; Over- or under-processing: a lift or lamination can turn frizzy, kinked or too weak, or set unevenly; Skin reactions to wax: redness, lifting or tenderness, bumps, ingrown hairs, rarely a burn or bruise; Uneven color or shape: tint and henna take differently on each hair and skin type and fade at their own pace; Retention varies: hormones, oily skin, steam, sleep habits and aftercare all change how long lashes last; Tool injury: a slip of tweezers or scissors near the eye is rare but possible if you move suddenly; Product in the eye: flushed right away with sterile saline; seek eye care if pain or blurred vision lasts. Tinting note: in the US, no color additive is FDA-approved for dyeing lashes or brows. Any tint or henna is used off-label at your informed choice, after a patch test. Some states restrict lash and brow tinting. Results depend on your natural lashes and brows, growth cycle, skin oiliness, hormones, medications, lifestyle and how closely you follow aftercare. Lashes shed naturally every day, so extensions need regular fills. I understand these risks.","type":"Yes / No","required":true},{"id":"lb-service-consent-6","label":"I've read the risks above and had my questions answered. No specific result has been promised to me.","type":"Yes / No","required":true},{"id":"lb-service-consent-7","label":"My health history is true and complete, and I've listed all medications, eye drops and lash serums.","type":"Yes / No","required":true},{"id":"lb-service-consent-8","label":"I'll remove contact lenses, keep my eyes closed and still, and tell you right away if anything stings or burns.","type":"Yes / No","required":true},{"id":"lb-service-consent-9","label":"I approved my lash or brow design, length, curl or shade before the service started.","type":"Yes / No","required":true},{"id":"lb-service-consent-10","label":"I've completed a patch test, or I've signed the patch test waiver and accept the added risk.","type":"Yes / No","required":true},{"id":"lb-service-consent-11","label":"I'll follow aftercare and contact you, and a healthcare provider, if signs of infection or allergy appear.","type":"Yes / No","required":true},{"id":"lb-service-consent-12","label":"I won't remove extensions myself. Removal by a professional may cost extra.","type":"Yes / No","required":true},{"id":"lb-service-consent-13","label":"I release {business} from claims caused by details I withheld or aftercare I skipped, as state law allows.","type":"Yes / No","required":true},{"id":"lb-service-consent-14","label":"I am 18 or older, not under the influence of alcohol or drugs, and signing of my own free will.","type":"Yes / No","required":true},{"id":"lb-service-consent-15","label":"I confirm the information above is accurate","type":"Signature","required":true}]},
"lb-patch":{"name":"Patch test consent & record","qs":[{"id":"lb-patch-1","label":"Client name","type":"Short text","required":true},{"id":"lb-patch-2","label":"Phone","type":"Short text","required":false},{"id":"lb-patch-3","label":"Planned service","type":"Short text","required":false},{"id":"lb-patch-4","label":"Known allergies or sensitivities","type":"Short text","required":false},{"id":"lb-patch-5","label":"Appointment date","type":"Date","required":false},{"id":"lb-patch-6","label":"ABOUT YOUR PATCH TEST. Each planned product is tested before your first service and checked at 24 and 48 hours. Adhesive: a few extensions at the outer corner, or a dot behind the ear. Tint or henna: behind the ear or inner elbow, 48 hours ahead and whenever the product changes. Lift or lamination solution: behind the ear. A clear test can't rule out a future reaction; adhesive sensitivity can develop after many sets. I have read this.","type":"Yes / No","required":true},{"id":"lb-patch-7","label":"Your choice","type":"Single select","required":true,"options":["I consent to this patch test","I decline the patch test"]},{"id":"lb-patch-8","label":"IF YOU CONSENT. If the spot burns, blisters, swells or itches badly, I'll wash it with cool water and call {phone|you}. If I have trouble breathing or swelling of the face or throat, I'll call 911.","type":"Yes / No","required":false},{"id":"lb-patch-9","label":"IF YOU DECLINE. I was offered a patch test and chose not to have one. I understand this means an allergy to the lash adhesive, tint, henna or lift solution won't be found before my service, and that a reaction could cause eyelid or skin swelling, need medical care, or mean my extensions have to be removed. I accept these risks and release {business} from claims related to a reaction a patch test might have shown, as far as state law allows.","type":"Yes / No","required":false},{"id":"lb-patch-10","label":"I confirm the information above is accurate","type":"Signature","required":true}]},
"lb-photo":{"name":"Lash & brow photo release","qs":[{"id":"lb-photo-1","label":"Client name","type":"Short text","required":true},{"id":"lb-photo-2","label":"Phone","type":"Short text","required":false},{"id":"lb-photo-3","label":"Email","type":"Short text","required":false},{"id":"lb-photo-4","label":"Clinical record: before and after photos in my private file to plan styling and track retention. Never shared.","type":"Yes / No","required":true},{"id":"lb-photo-5","label":"Portfolio, before and after: shown on your website, in print or in a studio portfolio book to show your work.","type":"Yes / No","required":false},{"id":"lb-photo-6","label":"Social media: posted on your business social accounts, including short videos and reels.","type":"Yes / No","required":false},{"id":"lb-photo-7","label":"How much of my face may be shown (if yes to portfolio or social). You may see any image before it is posted.","type":"Single select","required":false,"options":["Eyes closed, lashes or brows only","Eyes and brows, face cropped","Full face visible"]},{"id":"lb-photo-8","label":"Testimonial, name or tag: you may quote my review, use my first name, or tag my social handle with my photos.","type":"Yes / No","required":false},{"id":"lb-photo-9","label":"Name or handle to use (if yes above)","type":"Short text","required":false},{"id":"lb-photo-10","label":"Limits (areas, platforms, dates)","type":"Short text","required":false},{"id":"lb-photo-11","label":"HOW YOUR PHOTOS ARE HANDLED. Storage: kept on a business device in our secure app, never a personal camera roll, for 7 years. Changing your mind: text or email to withdraw; posts we control come down within 7 days; others' shares may be out of reach. No payment: this release is voluntary; you won't receive payment, royalties or free services for photos or reviews. Honest images: no filters, retouching or digitally added lashes; same lighting and angle for before and after. Lash close-ups are usually taken with your eyes closed; tell us any time if you'd rather not be filmed. I have read this.","type":"Yes / No","required":true},{"id":"lb-photo-12","label":"By signing, I confirm my choices above. This release stays in effect until I change or withdraw it in writing.","type":"Signature","required":true}]},
"lb-policy":{"name":"Lash & brow booking policy","qs":[{"id":"lb-policy-1","label":"Client name","type":"Short text","required":true},{"id":"lb-policy-2","label":"Appointment date","type":"Date","required":false},{"id":"lb-policy-3","label":"BOOKING POLICY. Lash and brow appointments are reserved just for you, and some take up to 2.5 hours. Deposit: $25–50, due at booking to hold your time; non-refundable and applied to your total. Notice to change: 48 hours, to move your appointment and keep your deposit. Grace period: 15 minutes; after that, we may need to reschedule. Rescheduling: with 48 hours' notice, your deposit moves once; a second change needs a new deposit. No-show and late change: your deposit is forfeited; after 2 no-shows, a full prepayment is needed to book. Late arrival: after 15 minutes your service may be shortened (fewer lashes) or rescheduled, and the deposit is forfeited. Come prepared: arrive with clean lashes and brows, no eye makeup and contacts out; cleansing time comes out of your service. I have read this.","type":"Yes / No","required":true},{"id":"lb-policy-4","label":"FILLS & RESULTS. Fill window: fills are booked every 2–3 weeks and need at least 40% of your extensions remaining; less than that is priced as a new full set. Another artist's lashes: we don't fill another artist's work; it's removed and replaced with a new full set. Retention check: lashes lost in the first 72 hours due to application are replaced free; shedding, oils, steam or picking aren't covered. Lift and lamination: wait 6–8 weeks between services; a free re-do within 7 days applies only if the curl or set didn't take and aftercare was followed. Feeling unwell? Pink eye, a stye, cold or flu? Tell us as soon as you can and we'll reschedule with no fee. Refunds: services can't be refunded once performed; tell us about any concern within 72 hours so we can fix it. I have read this.","type":"Yes / No","required":true},{"id":"lb-policy-5","label":"My deposit is non-refundable, and I understand the fill window and the 40% rule.","type":"Yes / No","required":true},{"id":"lb-policy-6","label":"Lashes lost to skipped aftercare, oils, steam or picking aren't covered by the retention check.","type":"Yes / No","required":true},{"id":"lb-policy-7","label":"By signing, I confirm I've read and agree to this policy, including the non-refundable deposit and fill rules.","type":"Signature","required":true}]},
"lb-ext-consent":{"name":"Lash extension consent","qs":[{"id":"lb-ext-consent-1","label":"Client name","type":"Short text","required":true},{"id":"lb-ext-consent-2","label":"Artist","type":"Short text","required":false},{"id":"lb-ext-consent-3","label":"ABOUT THIS SERVICE. What it is: Single extensions (classic) or light fans (volume, hybrid) bonded to your natural lashes with adhesive. What to expect: About 1.5 to 2.5 hours lying down with eyes closed. Under-eye pads protect your lower lashes. How long it lasts: Extensions shed with your natural lashes. Fills every 2 to 3 weeks keep the set full. I have read this.","type":"Yes / No","required":true},{"id":"lb-ext-consent-4","label":"POSSIBLE RISKS AND SIDE EFFECTS. Allergy to adhesive: puffy, itchy or red eyelids; Allergy can start after many sets without issue; Red or watery eyes from adhesive fumes, short-lived; Eye irritation if pads or tape shift; Infection, more likely without daily cleansing; Natural lash damage from extensions that are too heavy; Lash loss from picking, pulling or home removal; Minor eye injury from tools, which is rare. Shedding 1 to 5 natural lashes a day is normal; extensions come out with them. That is not lash damage. I understand these risks.","type":"Yes / No","required":true},{"id":"lb-ext-consent-5","label":"Quick health check: check anything that applies to you.","type":"Contraindications","required":false,"items":["Eye infection, stye or pink eye","Blepharitis or dry eye flare","Eye or eyelid surgery, LASIK","Allergy to adhesive or glue","Sensitive skin, eczema near eyes","Allergy to latex or tape","Pregnant or breastfeeding","Chemo, now or recently","Alopecia or trichotillomania","Lash serum or glaucoma drops","Contact lenses (remove today)","Asthma or fume sensitivity","Lash lift or tint in the past 2 weeks","Another artist's extensions on","Trouble lying flat for 2 hours"]},{"id":"lb-ext-consent-6","label":"If you checked anything, tell us more","type":"Long text","required":false},{"id":"lb-ext-consent-7","label":"STYLE APPROVAL. We agreed on my style, length and curl; my artist may adjust to protect my lashes.","type":"Yes / No","required":true},{"id":"lb-ext-consent-8","label":"I've shared my full health and eye history honestly, and will tell my artist about any changes.","type":"Yes / No","required":true},{"id":"lb-ext-consent-9","label":"I'll keep my eyes closed throughout and tell my artist right away about stinging, burning or discomfort.","type":"Yes / No","required":true},{"id":"lb-ext-consent-10","label":"I was offered an adhesive patch test. A clear test doesn't rule out a reaction later.","type":"Yes / No","required":true},{"id":"lb-ext-consent-11","label":"If my eyelids swell, itch or turn red, I'll contact my artist and have the set removed professionally.","type":"Yes / No","required":true},{"id":"lb-ext-consent-12","label":"I'll follow my aftercare. Retention varies with skin, hormones and habits, and isn't guaranteed.","type":"Yes / No","required":true},{"id":"lb-ext-consent-13","label":"I won't pick, pull or remove extensions myself. This can take my natural lashes out with them.","type":"Yes / No","required":true},{"id":"lb-ext-consent-14","label":"Fills need 40% of extensions left, or a full set is charged. Fees follow {business} policy.","type":"Yes / No","required":true},{"id":"lb-ext-consent-15","label":"Before and after photos for my private record are OK. Social media use only with my separate OK.","type":"Yes / No","required":true},{"id":"lb-ext-consent-16","label":"By signing, I confirm I am 18 or older with photo ID (or have parent or guardian consent per our policy and local law), have read this form, had my questions answered, and consent to lash extensions and future fills.","type":"Signature","required":true}]},
"lb-lift-consent":{"name":"Lash lift & tint consent","qs":[{"id":"lb-lift-consent-1","label":"Client name","type":"Short text","required":true},{"id":"lb-lift-consent-2","label":"Artist","type":"Short text","required":false},{"id":"lb-lift-consent-3","label":"ABOUT THIS SERVICE. What it is: A lifting solution and setting lotion curl your natural lashes over a silicone shield. Tint is optional. What to expect: About 45 to 75 minutes lying back with your eyes closed the whole time. Contacts come out first. How long it lasts: Usually 6 to 8 weeks, as new lashes grow in. Wait at least 6 to 8 weeks between lifts. I have read this.","type":"Yes / No","required":true},{"id":"lb-lift-consent-4","label":"POSSIBLE RISKS AND SIDE EFFECTS. Over-processing: frizzy, kinked or crimped lashes; Under-processing: a weak or short-lived curl; Lash dryness or breakage, more so if lashes are fine; An uneven curl between eyes or across the lash line; Stinging, redness or watery eyes from the solution; Solution or tint getting into the eye; Allergic reaction to lift solution or tint, even later; Light skin staining from tint, usually gone in 1–2 days. I understand these risks.","type":"Yes / No","required":true},{"id":"lb-lift-consent-5","label":"Quick health check: check anything that applies to you.","type":"Contraindications","required":false,"items":["Eye infection, stye or pink eye now","Eye or eyelid surgery in the past 3 months","Lash extensions on now","Lift or lash perm in the past 6–8 weeks","Lash serum (e.g. bimatoprost)","Glaucoma or other eye drops","Allergy to tint, PPD or lift solution","Contact lenses","Dry eye or blepharitis","Rash, eczema or sunburn near eyes","Pregnant or breastfeeding","Chemotherapy, now or recent","Trichotillomania or alopecia","Very short, sparse or fragile lashes","Very sensitive or watery eyes"]},{"id":"lb-lift-consent-6","label":"If you checked anything, tell us more","type":"Long text","required":false},{"id":"lb-lift-consent-7","label":"ABOUT LASH TINT. In the US, no color additive is FDA-approved for tinting eyelashes or eyebrows and FDA has reported serious eye injuries from tints, so any tint is used off-label, at my informed choice, after a patch test. My choice:","type":"Single select","required":true,"options":["Tint, please","Lift only"]},{"id":"lb-lift-consent-8","label":"I've shared my full health, eye, medication and lash serum history honestly, and will report any changes.","type":"Yes / No","required":true},{"id":"lb-lift-consent-9","label":"I understand the risks above. My curl depends on my lashes and their growth stage, and isn't guaranteed.","type":"Yes / No","required":true},{"id":"lb-lift-consent-10","label":"I'll keep my eyes closed and tell my artist right away if I feel stinging, burning or anything unusual.","type":"Yes / No","required":true},{"id":"lb-lift-consent-11","label":"I had a patch test with no reaction, or I declined it and signed the patch test waiver.","type":"Yes / No","required":true},{"id":"lb-lift-consent-12","label":"I won't have another lift sooner than 6 to 8 weeks; lifting too soon can over-process and break lashes.","type":"Yes / No","required":true},{"id":"lb-lift-consent-13","label":"I'll follow my aftercare. Water, steam or mascara in the first 24 hours can weaken or drop the curl.","type":"Yes / No","required":true},{"id":"lb-lift-consent-14","label":"Before and after photos for my private record are required. Social media use only with my separate OK.","type":"Yes / No","required":true},{"id":"lb-lift-consent-15","label":"Deposits and fees follow {business} policy. Re-dos only as stated in our re-do policy.","type":"Yes / No","required":true},{"id":"lb-lift-consent-16","label":"By signing, I confirm I am 18 or older with photo ID (or have parent or guardian consent per our policy and local law), have read this form, had my questions answered, and consent to a lash lift and any tint I chose above.","type":"Signature","required":true}]},
"lb-lam-consent":{"name":"Brow lamination consent","qs":[{"id":"lb-lam-consent-1","label":"Client name","type":"Short text","required":true},{"id":"lb-lam-consent-2","label":"Artist","type":"Short text","required":false},{"id":"lb-lam-consent-3","label":"ABOUT THIS SERVICE. What it is: Lifting and setting lotions reshape brow hairs so they sit brushed up and fuller. Tint is optional. What to expect: About 45 to 60 minutes. Any tweezing, waxing or threading comes after lamination. How long it lasts: Usually 6 to 8 weeks, as new hairs grow in. Wait at least 6 to 8 weeks between laminations. I have read this.","type":"Yes / No","required":true},{"id":"lb-lam-consent-4","label":"POSSIBLE RISKS AND SIDE EFFECTS. Over-processing: frizzy, fluffy or brittle hairs; Under-processing: hairs that drop back quickly; Dryness or breakage, more so if hairs are fine; An uneven set between brows or within a brow; Skin redness, stinging or dryness under the brows; Solution or tint running toward the eye; Allergic reaction to the solution or tint, even later; Skin staining from tint, usually gone in 1–2 days. I understand these risks.","type":"Yes / No","required":true},{"id":"lb-lam-consent-5","label":"Quick health check: check anything that applies to you.","type":"Contraindications","required":false,"items":["Eye infection or irritation now","Brow lamination in the past 6–8 weeks","Brow PMU healing (under 6 weeks)","Accutane in the past 6 months","Retinoids or acids on brows in the past 7 days","Peel, laser or microneedling in the past 2 weeks","Allergy to tint, PPD or lift solution","Botox near brows in the past 48 hours","Blood thinners or easy bruising","Broken skin, rash or sunburn","Pregnant or breastfeeding","Chemotherapy, now or recent","Trichotillomania or alopecia","Very fine, sparse or fragile brow hair","Very sensitive or reactive skin"]},{"id":"lb-lam-consent-6","label":"If you checked anything, tell us more","type":"Long text","required":false},{"id":"lb-lam-consent-7","label":"ABOUT BROW TINT. In the US, no color additive is FDA-approved for tinting eyelashes or eyebrows and FDA has reported serious eye injuries from tints, so any tint is used off-label, at my informed choice, after a patch test. My choice:","type":"Single select","required":true,"options":["Tint, please","Lamination only"]},{"id":"lb-lam-consent-8","label":"I've shared my full health, medication and skincare history honestly, and will report any changes.","type":"Yes / No","required":true},{"id":"lb-lam-consent-9","label":"I understand the risks above. Results depend on my brow hair and how it grows, and aren't guaranteed.","type":"Yes / No","required":true},{"id":"lb-lam-consent-10","label":"I'll keep my eyes closed when asked and say right away if I feel stinging, burning or anything unusual.","type":"Yes / No","required":true},{"id":"lb-lam-consent-11","label":"I had a patch test with no reaction, or I declined it and signed the patch test waiver.","type":"Yes / No","required":true},{"id":"lb-lam-consent-12","label":"I won't laminate again sooner than 6 to 8 weeks; doing it too soon can over-process and break brow hairs.","type":"Yes / No","required":true},{"id":"lb-lam-consent-13","label":"I'll follow my aftercare. Water, sweat, steam or brow makeup in the first 24 hours can weaken the set.","type":"Yes / No","required":true},{"id":"lb-lam-consent-14","label":"Before and after photos for my private record are required. Social media use only with my separate OK.","type":"Yes / No","required":true},{"id":"lb-lam-consent-15","label":"Deposits and fees follow {business} policy. Re-dos only as stated in our re-do policy.","type":"Yes / No","required":true},{"id":"lb-lam-consent-16","label":"By signing, I confirm I am 18 or older with photo ID (or have parent or guardian consent per our policy and local law), have read this form, had my questions answered, and consent to brow lamination, tidying, and any tint I chose above.","type":"Signature","required":true}]},
"lb-tint-consent":{"name":"Brow tint & henna consent","qs":[{"id":"lb-tint-consent-1","label":"Client name","type":"Short text","required":true},{"id":"lb-tint-consent-2","label":"Service: tint or henna","type":"Short text","required":false},{"id":"lb-tint-consent-3","label":"ABOUT THIS SERVICE. What it is: Brow tint is a dye that colors the hairs. Henna brows color the hairs and stain the skin for a fuller look. What to expect: About 30 to 45 minutes, with shaping. A patch test 48 hours before is required. How long it lasts: Tint: hairs 3 to 6 weeks, skin 1 to 2 days. Henna: hairs 4 to 6 weeks, skin up to 2 weeks. I have read this.","type":"Yes / No","required":true},{"id":"lb-tint-consent-4","label":"POSSIBLE RISKS AND SIDE EFFECTS. Allergy to PPD or dye, even after past tints; Redness, itching or stinging on brow skin; A shade darker, warmer or cooler than expected; Uneven or patchy skin stain; Faster fading on oily skin or with exfoliants; Dye in the eye (rare), flushed at once. In the US, no color additive is FDA-approved for tinting brows or lashes (FDA has reported serious eye injuries from tints), so tint and henna are used off-label at your informed choice; some states restrict this service. I understand these risks.","type":"Yes / No","required":true},{"id":"lb-tint-consent-5","label":"Quick health check: check anything that applies to you.","type":"Contraindications","required":false,"items":["Allergy to hair dye, PPD or henna","Past reaction to a tint or patch test","Reaction to black henna","Eye infection, stye or pink eye","Eye or eyelid surgery in the past 3 months","Broken skin or sunburn on brows","Eczema or psoriasis near brows","Retinoids or acids in the past 7 days","Peel or laser in the past 2 weeks","Pregnant or breastfeeding","Chemotherapy now or recently","Alopecia or hair pulling in brows","Microblading or powder brows","Very sensitive skin or many allergies","Contact lenses (removed today)"]},{"id":"lb-tint-consent-6","label":"If you checked anything, tell us more","type":"Long text","required":false},{"id":"lb-tint-consent-7","label":"SHADE AND SHAPE APPROVAL. I've seen my shade and mapped brow shape in a mirror and approve both.","type":"Yes / No","required":true},{"id":"lb-tint-consent-8","label":"I've shared my full health, allergy, medication and skincare history honestly, and will report changes.","type":"Yes / No","required":true},{"id":"lb-tint-consent-9","label":"I had a patch test at least 48 hours ago, or signed the waiver. A clear test doesn't rule out a reaction.","type":"Yes / No","required":true},{"id":"lb-tint-consent-10","label":"I've read the note above about off-label use of brow tint and henna, and I choose to go ahead.","type":"Yes / No","required":true},{"id":"lb-tint-consent-11","label":"I understand the risks above. Color depends on my hair, skin and aftercare, and isn't guaranteed.","type":"Yes / No","required":true},{"id":"lb-tint-consent-12","label":"Brows look boldest on day one and soften. Henna skin stain fades over about 1 to 2 weeks.","type":"Yes / No","required":true},{"id":"lb-tint-consent-13","label":"I'll follow my aftercare. Water, oil cleansers, scrubs, acids and sun can fade color sooner.","type":"Yes / No","required":true},{"id":"lb-tint-consent-14","label":"Before and after photos may be taken for my private record. Social media use only with my separate OK.","type":"Yes / No","required":true},{"id":"lb-tint-consent-15","label":"Deposits and fees follow {business} policy. Services can't be refunded once performed.","type":"Yes / No","required":true},{"id":"lb-tint-consent-16","label":"By signing, I confirm I am 18 or older with photo ID (or have parent or guardian consent per our policy and local law), have read this form, had my questions answered, and consent to brow tint and/or henna brows.","type":"Signature","required":true}]},
"lb-wax-consent":{"name":"Brow wax & shaping consent","qs":[{"id":"lb-wax-consent-1","label":"Client name","type":"Short text","required":true},{"id":"lb-wax-consent-2","label":"Method: wax, tweeze or thread","type":"Short text","required":false},{"id":"lb-wax-consent-3","label":"ABOUT THIS SERVICE. What it is: Unwanted hairs are removed with warm wax, tweezers or a thread to give a clean, balanced shape. What to expect: About 15 to 30 minutes. Mild redness is common and usually settles within a few hours. How long it lasts: Usually 3 to 5 weeks, depending on your hair growth. Regular visits keep the shape tidy. I have read this.","type":"Yes / No","required":true},{"id":"lb-wax-consent-4","label":"POSSIBLE RISKS AND SIDE EFFECTS. Redness, tenderness or mild swelling; Skin lifting, mostly with retinoids; Burns if wax is too warm; Bruising, more likely on blood thinners; Breakouts or small bumps afterward; Ingrown hairs or folliculitis; A shape that isn't quite as expected; Allergy to wax, resin or after-products. Accutane in the past 6 months or a recent prescription retinoid? No wax; hairs are tweezed or threaded instead. I understand these risks.","type":"Yes / No","required":true},{"id":"lb-wax-consent-5","label":"Quick health check: check anything that applies to you.","type":"Contraindications","required":false,"items":["Isotretinoin in the past 6 months","Rx retinoid on face in the past 7 days","Retinol, AHA, BHA or scrub in the past 5 days","Peel, laser or microneedling in the past 2 weeks","Botox near brows in the past 48 hours","Sunburn or fresh tan on the area","Broken skin, rash or cold sore","Eczema, psoriasis or rosacea flare","Blood thinners or easy bruising","Diabetes or slow healing","Allergy to wax, resin or pine","Moles or skin tags near brows","Pregnant or breastfeeding","Eye or eyelid surgery in the past 3 months","New medication or antibiotics"]},{"id":"lb-wax-consent-6","label":"If you checked anything, tell us more","type":"Long text","required":false},{"id":"lb-wax-consent-7","label":"SHAPE APPROVAL. I've seen the mapped shape in a mirror and approve it before any hair is removed.","type":"Yes / No","required":true},{"id":"lb-wax-consent-8","label":"I've shared my full health, medication and skincare history, including retinoids and acne treatment.","type":"Yes / No","required":true},{"id":"lb-wax-consent-9","label":"I understand skin lifting and burns are more likely if anything above was left out or changes.","type":"Yes / No","required":true},{"id":"lb-wax-consent-10","label":"If my skin isn't suited to wax today, I agree to tweezing or threading instead.","type":"Yes / No","required":true},{"id":"lb-wax-consent-11","label":"I understand the risks above. Results and symmetry depend on my natural growth and aren't guaranteed.","type":"Yes / No","required":true},{"id":"lb-wax-consent-12","label":"Removed hairs take weeks to grow back, so a shape change can't be undone right away.","type":"Yes / No","required":true},{"id":"lb-wax-consent-13","label":"I'll follow my aftercare: no sun, heat, makeup or exfoliation on the area for 24 to 48 hours.","type":"Yes / No","required":true},{"id":"lb-wax-consent-14","label":"Before and after photos may be taken for my private record. Social media use only with my separate OK.","type":"Yes / No","required":true},{"id":"lb-wax-consent-15","label":"Deposits and fees follow {business} policy. Services can't be refunded once performed.","type":"Yes / No","required":true},{"id":"lb-wax-consent-16","label":"By signing, I confirm I am 18 or older with photo ID (or have parent or guardian consent per our policy and local law), have read this form, had my questions answered, and consent to brow shaping by wax, tweezing and/or threading.","type":"Signature","required":true}]},
"lb-removal-consent":{"name":"Lash removal consent","qs":[{"id":"lb-removal-consent-1","label":"Client name","type":"Short text","required":true},{"id":"lb-removal-consent-2","label":"Artist","type":"Short text","required":false},{"id":"lb-removal-consent-3","label":"ABOUT THIS SERVICE. What it is: Your extensions are dissolved off with a professional gel or cream remover. No pulling or oil soaking. What to expect: About 20 to 45 minutes lying down with eyes closed. Under-eye pads protect your lower lashes. Afterward: Your natural lashes may look short or sparse at first. They regrow over the next 6 to 8 weeks. I have read this.","type":"Yes / No","required":true},{"id":"lb-removal-consent-4","label":"POSSIBLE RISKS AND SIDE EFFECTS. Redness or stinging from the remover, usually brief; Remover getting into the eye, which is flushed out; Watery eyes or mild eyelid puffiness for a short time; Allergy or sensitivity to the remover, which is rare; Some natural lashes coming away during removal; Lashes looking thin where extensions were heavy; Eye irritation if pads or tape shift; Infection, which is rare with clean tools. Lashes that come off during removal are usually ones that were already due to shed. Healthy lashes are not pulled out. I understand these risks.","type":"Yes / No","required":true},{"id":"lb-removal-consent-5","label":"Quick health check: check anything that applies to you.","type":"Contraindications","required":false,"items":["Eye infection, stye or pink eye","Blepharitis or dry eye flare","Eye or eyelid surgery, LASIK","Swelling or itching from lashes","Sensitive skin, eczema near eyes","Allergy to latex or tape","Known allergy to adhesive","Chemo, now or recently","Alopecia or trichotillomania","Lash serum or glaucoma drops","Contact lenses (remove today)","Asthma or fume sensitivity","Pregnant or breastfeeding","Another artist's extensions on","Trouble lying flat for 45 minutes"]},{"id":"lb-removal-consent-6","label":"If you checked anything, tell us more","type":"Long text","required":false},{"id":"lb-removal-consent-7","label":"REASON FOR REMOVAL. I've told my artist why I'm removing my set (reaction, grow-out, a break, new style).","type":"Yes / No","required":true},{"id":"lb-removal-consent-8","label":"I've shared my full health and eye history honestly, including any reaction to my current set.","type":"Yes / No","required":true},{"id":"lb-removal-consent-9","label":"I'll keep my eyes closed throughout and tell my artist right away about stinging or burning.","type":"Yes / No","required":true},{"id":"lb-removal-consent-10","label":"My lashes may look shorter, thinner or uneven after removal. This is normal regrowth, not damage.","type":"Yes / No","required":true},{"id":"lb-removal-consent-11","label":"If I suspect an adhesive allergy, I'll see a doctor before having any new set applied.","type":"Yes / No","required":true},{"id":"lb-removal-consent-12","label":"If my lashes are weak, my artist may suggest a 4–6 week rest before any new set.","type":"Yes / No","required":true},{"id":"lb-removal-consent-13","label":"I won't soak, pick or pull at extensions at home, now or in the future.","type":"Yes / No","required":true},{"id":"lb-removal-consent-14","label":"Removal fees follow {business} policy, and services can't be refunded once performed.","type":"Yes / No","required":true},{"id":"lb-removal-consent-15","label":"Before and after photos for my private record are OK. Social media use only with my separate OK.","type":"Yes / No","required":true},{"id":"lb-removal-consent-16","label":"By signing, I confirm I am 18 or older with photo ID (or have parent or guardian consent per our policy and local law), have read this form, had my questions answered, and consent to professional lash extension removal.","type":"Signature","required":true}]}};
const LB_GUIDES=[{"id":"g-lb-ext","icon":"👁️","title":"Caring for your lash extensions","cat":"Aftercare","profs":["lash"],"tips":["Your lashes are bonded one by one, and the adhesive keeps curing for the first day or two. A little daily care keeps them full, comfortable and lasting longer.","First 24–48 hours (adhesive curing). Normal: lashes may feel slightly stiff or heavy, and a faint adhesive smell is normal. Do: keep lashes dry for 24 hours, brush gently with a clean spoolie morning and night, sleep on your back or side. Avoid: water, steam, saunas, hot showers on your face and sweaty workouts for 48 hours, and rubbing or touching.","First week (settling in). Normal: lashes soften and settle; a few may twist, and brushing fixes most. Do: start cleansing daily with lash-safe foam, rinse, pat dry, then brush through; remove makeup with oil-free remover. Avoid: oil-based cleansers, balms or eye creams near lashes, mascara and lash curlers, and picking at a stray lash.","Weeks 2–3 (fill time). Normal: natural shedding leaves gaps, mostly at the outer corners. Do: keep cleansing and brushing daily, and come to your fill with clean lashes and no eye makeup. Avoid: waiting too long between fills, and pulling out lashes that are growing out or twisted.","Every day. Normal: 1 to 5 natural lashes shed each day, taking their extensions with them. Do: cleanse daily, brush often, sleep on your back or side, book fills every 2 to 3 weeks. Avoid: removing extensions at home, and oils, steam and rubbing, which shorten retention.","About shedding: each lash grows in about 6 to 8 weeks, then falls out naturally. Finding a few lashes on your pillow is normal and is not a sign of damage.","Keep it dry for the first 24 hours. Cleanse daily with lash-safe foam. Skip the oils, since oil breaks down adhesive. Hands off: no picking, pulling or rubbing. Brush instead.","Call me right away if you notice: puffy, itchy or red eyelids, even days later; a rash on the lids or around the eyes; yellow or green discharge or crusting; redness or soreness that keeps getting worse. For swelling, itching or a rash, the set needs to come off professionally; see your doctor too.","Eye pain or vision changes: get urgent eye care. Trouble breathing or face or throat swelling: call 911.","Questions? Text {phone|me} · {business}"]},
{"id":"g-lb-lift","icon":"✨","title":"Caring for your lash lift","cat":"Aftercare","profs":["lash"],"tips":["The first 24 hours set your curl. After that, a little daily care keeps your lashes lifted, healthy and soft for 6 to 8 weeks.","First 24 hours (the curl sets). Normal: a strong, very curled look that softens in a day or two; tint may leave a faint shadow on the skin. Do: keep lashes completely dry, sleep on your back, leave them alone. Avoid: water, steam, showers on your face, sweat, mascara, eye makeup and rubbing your eyes.","Days 2–7 (settling in). Normal: the curl relaxes into a natural lift; a stray lash or two may point a different way. Do: brush lashes up each morning with a clean spoolie and start a non-prostaglandin lash conditioner. Avoid: oil-based removers or cleansers near eyes, waterproof mascara and lash curlers.","Weeks 2–6 (enjoy it). Normal: the lift holds well, tint slowly softens, and new straight lashes start to grow in. Do: water-based mascara only, removed gently; keep conditioning nightly and brushing daily. Avoid: pulling, picking or tugging at lashes, and harsh scrubs or acids around your eyes.","Weeks 6–8 (next lift). Normal: the curl grows out with your natural lash cycle, so mixed straight and curled lashes are normal. Do: book your next lift and tint, and tell me about any new eye drops, serums or health changes. Avoid: lifting again sooner than 6 weeks, or a home perm kit; both can over-process lashes.","Good to know: contacts can go back in today unless eyes feel irritated; pools, sauna and steam rooms are fine after 24 hours; a nourishing lash conditioner keeps lashes soft; lash serums with prostaglandins can over-curl lashes; chlorine and sun can fade tint a little faster; use only gentle, oil-free eye makeup remover.","Call me right away if you notice: eyelid swelling, itching or a rash; redness that gets worse instead of better; discharge, crusting or a gritty feeling; lashes that feel brittle or are breaking.","Eye pain or any change in your vision: get urgent eye care today. Trouble breathing, or swelling of the face or throat: call 911.","Questions? Text {phone|me} · {business}"]},
{"id":"g-lb-lam","icon":"🪮","title":"Caring for laminated brows","cat":"Aftercare","profs":["brow"],"tips":["The first 24 hours set your brows. After that, a little daily brushing and oil keeps them full, soft and in place for 6 to 8 weeks.","First 24 hours (brows are setting). Normal: brows look very upright and set and may feel stiff; tint can leave a light skin stain for 1–2 days. Do: keep brows completely dry, sleep on your back, try not to touch, rub or brush them yet. Avoid: water, steam, sweat, workouts, brow makeup and any face products on your brows.","Days 2–7 (settling in). Normal: hairs soften and settle; brows can feel a little dry and a few hairs may stray. Do: brush brows into shape each morning, and from day 2 use a drop of nourishing brow oil nightly. Avoid: steam and heavy sweat until 48 hours, and extra waxing or tweezing until 48 hours.","Weeks 2–6 (enjoy it). Normal: the shape holds well, tint slowly softens, new hairs grow in at their own angle. Do: keep brushing daily and oiling at night; brow gel helps hold stray hairs. Avoid: retinoids, acids, scrubs and peels on your brows, tanning beds and long sun without SPF.","Weeks 6–8 (next visit). Normal: brows gradually return to their natural direction. Do: book your next lamination and tell me about any new skincare, medication or health changes. Avoid: laminating again sooner than 6 weeks, or a home kit; both can over-process brow hairs.","Good to know: brows can look a little fluffy for a day or two; sauna, steam rooms and hot yoga after 48 hours; use a clean spoolie and wash it every week; brow makeup and gel are fine after 24 hours; sun, chlorine and oily skin fade tint faster; tint lasts about 3–6 weeks on the hairs.","Call me right away if you notice: itching, a rash or bumps on or near the brows; redness or burning that gets worse; blistering, oozing or crusting skin; swelling around the brows or eyelids.","Eye pain or any change in your vision: get urgent eye care today. Trouble breathing, or swelling of the face or throat: call 911.","Questions? Text {phone|me} · {business}"]},
{"id":"g-lb-tint","icon":"🎨","title":"Caring for your tinted brows","cat":"Aftercare","profs":["brow"],"tips":["Brow tint colors your hairs, and henna also stains the skin underneath. Here's what to expect, and how to keep your color fresh for longer.","First 24–48 hours (keep dry). Normal: brows look bolder and more defined than they will settle; a little pinkness from shaping fades within hours. Do: keep brows dry for 24 hours (henna: 24 to 48); wash around them with a damp cloth and pat, don't rub. Avoid: brow makeup for 24 hours, steam, saunas, sweaty workouts, swimming and oil cleansers.","Days 2–14 (skin stain fades). Normal: tint stain on the skin is gone in 1 to 2 days; henna stain fades gradually over up to 2 weeks, faster on oily skin. Do: cleanse gently with a mild, oil-free cleanser and pat dry; brow pencil or gel is fine. Avoid: scrubs, peels, retinol, AHA or BHA on your brows, and rubbing them with a towel.","Weeks 3–6 (hair color fades). Normal: hair color softens and new hairs grow in uncolored; tint lasts about 3 to 6 weeks, henna about 4 to 6. Do: rebook for fresh color and a tidy-up, and shade your brows from strong sun. Avoid: box dyes or home tint kits near your eyes.","If you had brow tint: it colors the hairs only. Skin stain 1 to 2 days, hair color about 3 to 6 weeks. If you had henna brows: it colors hairs and stains skin for a filled-in look. Skin stain up to 2 weeks, hair color about 4 to 6 weeks.","Good to know: sun, tanning beds, chlorine and salt water fade color; oily skin holds the skin stain for less time; retinol and acids near brows fade color quickly; a reaction can happen even after past tints; we patch test again if the product changes.","Call me right away if you notice: itching, burning or redness that gets worse; swelling of your brows or eyelids; a rash, bumps or blisters on or near your brows; oozing, crusting or skin that feels hot. Color in your eye: rinse with clean water.","Eye pain or vision change: urgent eye care. Trouble breathing, or swelling of the face or throat: call 911.","Questions? Text {phone|me} · {business}"]},
{"id":"g-lb-shape","icon":"🌿","title":"Caring for your shaped brows","cat":"Aftercare","profs":["brow"],"tips":["Freshly shaped brows can look a little pink at first. Here's how to keep your skin calm and your shape clean until your next visit.","First 24 hours (calm skin). Normal: pinkness, mild swelling or tiny bumps around your brows, usually settling within a few hours. Do: use a cool compress or a little aloe gel, keep your hands off, sleep on a clean pillowcase. Avoid: makeup on the area for 12 to 24 hours, touching or picking, hot showers on your face and sun.","Days 2–3 (skin settles). Normal: skin looks normal again; a few small bumps can appear where hairs were removed and fade on their own. Do: cleanse gently and pat dry; a light, fragrance-free moisturizer keeps skin comfortable. Avoid: sun, tanning, saunas, steam and exfoliation for 48 hours, and retinol and acids on the area.","Weeks 3–5 (next shape). Normal: new hairs grow back at different rates; some fuzz around the shape is normal regrowth. Do: book your next shape and let strays grow so there are hairs to work with. Avoid: tweezing at home between visits; it's easy to over-pluck and lose the shape.","If you were waxed: wax lifts hairs from the root along with a thin layer of surface skin, so skip sun and exfoliation for 48 hours. If you were tweezed or threaded: gentler on the skin, but the follicles are open, so keep makeup, sweat and fingers away for 12 to 24 hours.","Good to know: redness usually settles within a few hours; bruising is more likely on blood thinners; brush brows into place with a clean spoolie; tell me about new retinoids or acne medication; prone to ingrowns? exfoliate gently after 48 hours; book every 3 to 5 weeks to keep your shape.","Call me right away if you notice: redness or swelling that gets worse after a day; skin that lifted, blistered or weeps; pus, crusting or bumps that keep growing; skin that feels hot, or a fever; hives or a spreading rash.","Eye pain or vision change: urgent eye care. Trouble breathing, or swelling of the face or throat: call 911.","Questions? Text {phone|me} · {business}"]},
{"id":"g-lb-removal","icon":"🌱","title":"After your lash removal","cat":"Aftercare","profs":["lash"],"tips":["Your natural lashes are free again. They may look shorter or sparser than you remember for a few weeks. That's normal regrowth, not damage.","Today (just removed). Normal: lashes may look short, thin or uneven; eyes can be a little pink or watery for a few hours. Do: leave lashes alone to settle; if eyes feel irritated, rinse with cool water and rest them. Avoid: rubbing your eyes, eye makeup and curling your lashes; contacts if eyes feel irritated.","First week (settling). Normal: small gaps where extensions were heaviest, and a few lashes shedding each day. Do: cleanse lashes daily with a gentle lash-safe foam and brush through with a clean spoolie. Avoid: waterproof mascara and harsh removers, and picking at leftover bits; I can clean them for you.","Weeks 2–6 (regrowth). Normal: new lashes grow in over 6 to 8 weeks and fullness slowly returns. Do: optional non-prostaglandin conditioning serum; rest 4–6 weeks if lashes are weak. Avoid: starting a new set before lashes recover, especially after a reaction.","Lash regrowth: each lash takes about 6 to 8 weeks to grow in, and every lash is at a different stage, so fullness returns gradually. Shedding 1 to 5 lashes a day is normal.","After a reaction: if your set was removed because of swelling, itching or redness, please see your doctor before having any new lashes applied. Sensitivity to adhesive can return with every set.","Call me right away if you notice: redness, puffiness or itching that lasts past a day; a rash on the lids or around the eyes; yellow or green discharge or crusting; lashes falling out in clumps or patches.","Get urgent eye care right away for eye pain, vision changes or ongoing light sensitivity. Trouble breathing, or swelling of the face or throat: call 911.","Questions? Text {phone|me} · {business}"]},
{"id":"g-lb-prep","icon":"📅","title":"Before your lash & brow visit","cat":"Pre-care","profs":["lash","brow"],"tips":["A little prep helps your service last longer and keeps your eyes and skin comfortable. Follow the timeline for your service.","6 months before: took isotretinoin (Accutane) in the last 6 months? No wax; I'll tweeze or thread. Eye surgery (LASIK, cataract, eyelid)? Wait 3 months and get your eye doctor's OK.","2 weeks before: for waxing, no chemical peels, laser or microneedling near the brows. Using a lash serum or glaucoma drops? Tell me now.","1 week before: for waxing, pause prescription retinoids (tretinoin, adapalene) near the brows. Let any sunburn on the area heal fully.","3–5 days before: pause retinol, AHA/BHA acids and scrubs near the brows. No oil-based eye products or cleansers.","48 hours before: patch test done for tint, henna, lift solution or lash adhesive. Had Botox near the brows? Wait 48 hours to wax.","Day of your visit: clean lashes and brows, no mascara, eye makeup or brow products. Contacts out; wear your glasses. Twitchy eyes? Skip the extra coffee.","Lash extensions: come with clean, dry lashes and no oils on the eyes for 24 hours. A full set takes 1.5–2.5 hours with eyes closed, so get comfy. Wearing another artist's set? Tell me; it may need removal first. Bring a photo of the look you like.","Lift and lamination: your last lift or lamination should be at least 6–8 weeks ago. Lash extensions must come off before a lift. Using a lash serum? Tell me; it changes how a lift takes. Don't wax or tweeze your brows first; I tidy them after lamination.","Tint, henna and wax: patch test 48 hours before your first tint and whenever products change. Let brows grow for 1–2 weeks so I can see your natural shape. Bring a photo of brows you love. Wax over recent retinoids can lift skin, so follow the timeline.","Please call to reschedule if you have: pink eye, a stye or any eye infection; red, itchy or swollen eyes or eyelids; a sunburn, rash or broken skin in the area; a fever, cold or flu; any redness or itching from your patch test; recent eye surgery without your eye doctor's OK. We ask for 48 hours' notice, but if it's about your safety, just call.","Pregnant or breastfeeding? It's not an automatic no, but hormones can change how lifts and extensions take, so check with your doctor and tell me. Never stop a prescribed medication without your doctor's OK.","Questions? Text {phone|me} · {business}"]},
{"id":"g-lb-retention","icon":"🔁","title":"Lash care & retention guide","cat":"Aftercare","profs":["lash"],"tips":["Healthy natural lashes hold extensions best. Here's how the lash cycle works, what affects retention and how to keep your set clean between fills.","Growth cycle: growing (about 30–45 days), a new lash grows in and extensions on these grow out fastest; transition (2–3 weeks), the lash stops growing and its root loosens; resting (up to about 100 days), the lash sits until it sheds with its extension. Each lash is on its own schedule, so shedding is steady, never all at once.","What helps and what hurts retention: oil-based cleansers, creams and makeup weaken the bond; saunas and steam soften adhesive, most in the first 48 hours; sleep on your back or side, since rubbing and picking pull lashes out; oily skin, hormones and some medications can shorten wear.","Cleansing, daily from 24 hours after: 1. Close your eyes and wet lashes with clean, lukewarm water. 2. One pump of lash-safe, oil-free foam; brush gently downward with a soft lash brush. 3. Rinse well so no cleanser is left at the base. 4. Pat dry with a lint-free towel, then brush through with a clean spoolie.","Normal shedding: 1–5 natural lashes a day; a new lash takes about 6–8 weeks to grow in. Retention check: lashes lost within 72 hours of your set due to application are replaced free. Fill schedule: every 2–3 weeks, with at least 40% of extensions left, or it's a full set.","Keep it dry: no water for 24 hours, no steam for 48. Oil-free only near the eyes. No curlers; extension-safe mascara only. Never pull extensions off; book a removal.","This is normal: finding 1–5 lashes a day with extensions on; a few twisted or crossed lashes as they grow out; small gaps by week 2–3; slightly pink eye whites for a day after your set; lashes looking thin for a few weeks after removal; a little more shedding with seasonal changes.","Call me if you notice: swollen, itchy or puffy eyelids; a rash or redness on the lids or under-eye area; red eyes lasting more than 24–48 hours; discharge, crusting or a stye; an extension poking your eye; natural lashes falling out in clumps.","Call 911 for trouble breathing, or swelling of the face or throat. Get urgent eye care for eye pain or vision changes. Possible allergy? Have your extensions removed professionally and see a doctor before any new set.","Questions? Text {phone|me} · {business}"]}];
